<BaseLayout title="About ChinookDB — Source and licence" description="Learn about the canonical Chinook Database source, attribution, MIT licence, and the independent ChinookDB hosted resource.">
  <section class="page-intro shell"><p class="eyebrow">About this resource</p><h1>Useful, open, independent.</h1><p>ChinookDB.com hosts the Chinook sample database for convenient use in learning, exploration, testing, and examples.</p></section>
  <section class="shell section about-grid"><article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">The source</p><h2>Chinook, by Luis Rocha</h2><p>The database models a digital music store with artists, albums, tracks, playlists, customers, employees, invoices, and invoice lines. The data and schema on this site are generated from the canonical SQLite fixture in the upstream project.</p><p>This website is an independent hosted resource. It is not the official upstream Chinook project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by its maintainers.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={source.repository}>View the upstream project on GitHub ↗</a></p><div class="source-details"><div><span>Upstream revision</span><code>{source.revision.slice(0, 12)}</code></div><div><span>Tables</span><strong>{tables.length}</strong></div><div><span>Licence</span><strong>MIT</strong></div></div></article><aside class="content-card licence-card"><p class="eyebrow">Licence</p><h2>MIT</h2><p>Copyright (c) 2008–2024 Luis Rocha</p><p>Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this software and associated documentation files, to deal in the software without restriction, including the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies.</p><p>The copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies or substantial portions of the software.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lerocha/chinook-database/blob/master/LICENSE.md">Read the full licence ↗</a></aside></section>
  <section class="shell section about-note"><p class="eyebrow">Licences</p><h2>The data keeps its upstream licence; this site's own work has two.</h2><p>The Chinook data is distributed under the upstream MIT licence shown above. Everything this site adds is licensed separately: the site code, the scripts and the ModelSpec model (<code>model/chinook.modelspec.hcl</code> and its generated JSON) are <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/datatug/chinookdb/blob/main/LICENSE">MIT</a>, and the model also carries the upstream MIT notice because it restates the upstream schema. The meaning file <code>model/chinook.meaning.yaml</code> is <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/datatug/chinookdb/blob/main/LICENSE-CC0">CC0-1.0</a>, and so are the universal concepts it reuses from <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/meaninggraph/core">meaninggraph/core</a>: copy them without attribution. Documentation under <code>docs/</code> and the generated checksum files are MIT.</p></section>
  <section class="shell section about-note"><p class="eyebrow">For the next milestone</p><h2>A straightforward path to interactive exploration.</h2><p>The static schema model and stable data URLs are intentionally easy to reuse in a future interactive Chinook explorer. DataTug is not integrated into this milestone.</p></section>
</BaseLayout>
